# history is rewritten (e.g. git filter-repo) — update them after any such
# rewrite by re-running `gitleaks detect` and copying the new fingerprints.
# `gitleaks detect` scans all local branches by default, so both the
# pre-rewrite hashes (still reachable via other, unrewritten branches) and
# the post-rewrite hashes (reachable via master) need an entry.
